record.authors_conclusion:
Partly right but too narrow. The authors conclude that:
- RL applied directly to pretraining checkpoints is effective from about 4B tokens and often matches SFT→RL on GSM8K;
- targeted pretraining data is a stronger lever for RL than model scale;
- direct RL expands pass@k, while sharpening appears only after SFT;
- SFT degrades general capabilities and RL does not;
- parallel averaging of RL and SFT updates gives the best pass@32;
- base pass@k may serve as a lightweight predictor of RL gains.
They draw no conclusions about loss scaling laws.
